# Intel: umbrelOS 2.0.2 in Docker on a DigitalOcean droplet. Last round's package installed and set up by its owner (a real person) on the owner's own Cloudflare domain at <name A>; Cloudflare's first sign-in came back as a browser download (cloudflare/cloudflared#1252), so the owner's cert.pem was copied into the cloudflared service's folder by hand; update.sh to this round (package at cdf4a58); the address moved to <name B> with a second sign-in (this one reached cloudflared normally); then owner moderation by hand (BUZZ_ADMIN_HOST=<name B>:8443 added to the installed compose file), probed from a Mac, and a ban made by the owner in Buzz Foundation 0.7.0-preview.270.2. Scripts: tests/umbrel/{server.py,install.sh,update.sh}; the session's page.sh, moderation.sh and member-post.sh.

